        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_963070105.1",
        "comments": "The assembly nxLitSigm11.1 is based on PacBio HiFi data (derived from a female Litomosoides sigmodontis individual) and Arima Hi-C data (derived from two pools of males and females) generated by the Wellcome Sanger Institute 959 Nematode Genomes project. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, and contamination removal via blobtoolkit. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, the assembly was scaffolded using YaHS and improved using manual curation. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size.",
